tasks.body:
Read contract ui.plugins-row-links v1 first — it carries the human's request verbatim, what free already built, and both fixes with their evidence. Two items, both Pro-side.

1) Dashboard link on Pro's own row. When both plugins are active your merge hides free's row, so free's own Dashboard link is unreachable — Pro's row has to carry one. Same shape as free's: prepend to plugin_action_links_{basename} AND network_admin_plugin_action_links_{basename} so Deactivate stays last, gate on the capability that can actually open the page, point at the free admin page. No upsell link on Pro's row.

2) The blank white square left of the merged FREE block at mobile. Cause is verified, not guessed: at <=782px core generates a pseudo-cell to stand in for the checkbox column (`.plugins .plugin-update-tr:before { content:''; display: table-cell }`) and only tints it when the row ABOVE has an update pending (`.active.update + .plugin-update-tr:before`). Pro's row is .active but not .update, so it stays unpainted. The block's own td is already tinted correctly — measured at 400px: td background rgba(56,88,233,0.08), ::before background rgba(0,0,0,0).

Fix, injected into the live page and photographed:

@media screen and (max-width: 782px) {
	.plugins .aissp-bundled-tr::before {
		background-color: rgba( var( --wp-admin-theme-color--rgb, 34, 113, 177 ), 0.08 );
		border-inline-start: 4px solid var( --wp-admin-theme-color, #72aee6 );
	}
}

Do not hard-code #f0f6fc / #72aee6. WP 7.0.2 (what the dev site runs) drives the plugins list from --wp-admin-theme-color; I tried the literals first and photographed the result — on the 'modern' scheme it paints a pale-blue slab and a teal bar next to a blue-violet row. The var() fallbacks are the 6.x literals so a pre-7.0 site degrades to today's look.

Free side is done and verified in-browser: row reads "Get Syncinator Pro | Dashboard | Deactivate", tab strip reads "Get [PRO]". Two things of yours it touches, neither breaking: the `tabs` filter descriptor may now carry an optional `badge: string` (additive; your get-pro removal already keys on tab.to), and free now reads `defined( 'AISSP_VERSION' )` to withhold the upsell while Pro runs — please keep defining that constant, and flag it here before any rename. Brand purple is #6f5d9e; your grey .aissp-bundled__badge stays grey, your own reasoning for why is now the rule.

tasks.note:
FIXED in free. ComparisonPanel now re-resolves the pending operation's row from the live `rows` on every render and passes that to SyncModal, falling back to the captured row if the slug has left the list. Fixed for ALL actions, not special-cased to backups — per pro's objection, which was right.

  const liveOperation = useMemo( () => {
      if ( ! sync.operation ) return null;
      const current = rows.find( ( row ) => row.slug === sync.operation.row.slug );
      return current ? { ...sync.operation, row: current } : sync.operation;
  }, [ sync.operation, rows ] );

So `row` and `backups` reaching the `sync:restore-version` slot are now live, and the confirm description follows the live row too.

Test: ComparisonPanel.test.jsx "follows the live row while the confirm dialog is open" — opens the restore dialog on backup 5.2, refetches to 9.9 with the dialog still up, asserts the dialog reads 9.9. VERIFIED TO FAIL WITHOUT THE FIX (reverted the one prop, test went red, restored it) — it is not a test that passes for the wrong reason.

Free: 553 Jest (+1), 804 PHPUnit, lint 0, bundle rebuilt.

Pro's spec workaround on 68-host-backup-history is still correct practice and needs no revert — waiting on observable panel state beats reading the DB either way.
